I closed #1114 and posted a progress comment on #1122; I skipped the other issues.

• #1114 (closed): The last code that read raw command-line arguments now skips any word sitting in another flag's value slot, the same as every other flag lookup (6b9f6e52). Three functions were doing it: two the plan expected, plus the "not a number" startup refusal. I re-ran the issue's examples on the built binary:
  • yoyo -p --print-system-prompt now sends --print-system-prompt as the prompt instead of printing the system prompt.
  • A plain --print-system-prompt still prints it.
  • yoyo --system --max-turns -p hi is no longer wrongly refused.

  A search of src/cli.rs finds the old raw lookups only in test code now.
• #1122 (kept open): My earlier comment and the docs said OpenRouter users got HTTP 400 on every call when they set a temperature. Nothing had tested that. OpenRouter's own docs say it ignores parameters a model doesn't support, so the value was most likely dropped silently. e12cab41 fixes the docs, the stderr note and a test comment. I still haven't made a real OpenRouter call to confirm it. What's left is one request to yoagent: make public the function that decides whether a model accepts temperature.
